-- akn:att_7__hc_1/p3 The table's file number; no rule.

§§ `בדיקת הנספחים`

`the 2016 salary tables` MEANS LIST `2016 annex א'1`, `2016 annex א'2`

`the 2016 conversion tables` MEANS
    LIST `2016 annex א'3`, `2016 annex א'4`, `2016 annex א'5`, `2016 annex א'6`, `2016 annex א'7`

`all seven 2016 tables` MEANS append `the 2016 salary tables` `the 2016 conversion tables`

#ASSERT count `all seven 2016 tables` EQUALS 7

-- (1) The conversion tables of existing teachers are the salary tables
-- with intermediate grades (the base agreement's §46(א)): every cell א'1
-- prints, א'3 (the B.A conversion, the same rating code 101) prints at the
-- same row and grade, and so א'5 (M.A, 102) for א'2.
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise in` `2016 annex א'1` `2016 annex א'3`)
#ASSERT null (`the cells printed otherwise in` `2016 annex א'2` `2016 annex א'5`)

-- (2) The steps each table prints: a row's 2% or 1% over the row above, a
-- grade's 7.5%, 7.8% or 8.5% over the grade before it. Each printed cell is
-- within an agora of the cell its step makes of its printed neighbour
-- (rounded to the agora, convention rounding.half); 1,409 of the 5,249
-- checks miss by an agora, none by more. No rule turns on the step, and
-- every cell is printed.
`all the 2016 step checks` MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN t YIELD `the percentage steps of` t) `all seven 2016 tables`)

#ASSERT count `all the 2016 step checks` EQUALS 5249
#ASSERT count (`the misses in` `all the 2016 step checks`) EQUALS 1409
#ASSERT null (`the cells off by more than` 1 `agorot in` `all the 2016 step checks`)

-- Grade 7 rises over grade 6 by 7.8% in every 2016 table, where the first
-- part's tables of 2011 printed 8.5%: the cells of grades 7–9 are lower
-- than the old steps made them, which is what the salary-protection
-- supplement of §7(ב) is for.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD elem (`grade step` 7 (7.8%)) (t's `grade steps`)) `all seven 2016 tables`
#ASSERT elem (`grade step` 7 (8.5%)) (`annex א1'`'s `grade steps`)

-- (3) An intermediate grade of a conversion table lies midway between the
-- grades around it, to the agora; no rule asks it.
GIVEN t IS A `salary table`, r IS A `table row`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cell check`
DECIDE `the intermediate grades of the 2016 row` t r IS
    concat (map (GIVEN c YIELD
                     IF c's grade EQUALS FLOOR (c's grade)
                     THEN EMPTY
                     ELSE `the midway check of` (r's `row place`) c (`the pay at grade` (c's grade MINUS 0.5) (r's `row cells`)) (`the pay at grade` (c's grade PLUS 0.5) (r's `row cells`)))
                (r's `row cells`))

GIVEN p IS A NUMBER, c IS A `grade cell`, below IS A MAYBE NUMBER, above IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `cell check`
DECIDE `the midway check of` p c below above IS
    CONSIDER below
    WHEN JUST lo THEN
        CONSIDER above
        WHEN JUST hi THEN LIST (`a check of` p (c's grade) (c's pay) (`to the agora` ((lo PLUS hi) DIVIDED BY 2)))
        WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY

`all the 2016 midway checks` MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN t YIELD concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD `the intermediate grades of the 2016 row` t r) (t's `rows`))) `the 2016 conversion tables`)

#ASSERT count `all the 2016 midway checks` EQUALS 1440
#ASSERT count (`the misses in` `all the 2016 midway checks`) EQUALS 336
#ASSERT null (`the cells off by more than` 1 `agorot in` `all the 2016 midway checks`)

-- (4) Every table rises along its grades and down its rows, so "the grade
-- nearest at or above A" (§46(ב)) is one cell.
#ASSERT all `rises along its grades and down its rows` `all seven 2016 tables`

-- The tables at work: §46's placement on a conversion row; the table
-- salary from the determining date, raised by a cost-of-living update.
#ASSERT `the placement in the row` 6000 (`the row labelled` `2016 annex א'3` 1) EQUALS JUST (`cell` 1.5 6023.36)
#ASSERT `the 2016 table salary on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) `2016 annex א'1` 36 9 EMPTY EQUALS JUST 15896.15
#ASSERT `the 2016 table salary on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2016) `2016 annex א'1` 36 9 EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the 2016 table salary on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2017) `2016 annex א'1` 1 1 (LIST `table update` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2017) (1%)) EQUALS JUST (5805.65 TIMES 1.01)
#ASSERT `the 2016 table salary on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) `2016 annex א'1` 1 2 EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
